## weight-in-lift

weight-in-lift-ask = When does the dynamometer in a lift show more or less?
weight-in-lift-title = A body’s weight in a lift
weight-in-lift-question = A dynamometer with four 100 g weights hangs under a lift cabin’s ceiling. We write down its readings while the lift stands, starts up, goes steadily, slows down, and then the same downwards. At last, the textbook’s investigation: we let the dynamometer go for a moment with its weights. When will the readings change?
weight-in-lift-choices = Only while the lift speeds up or slows down
weight-in-lift-choices-2 = More while the lift goes up, less while it goes down
weight-in-lift-choices-3 = Never: the weights’ mass is the same
weight-in-lift-setup = A lift cabin, a dynamometer (up to 5 N) under its ceiling, four 100 g weights
